DONE: reading is robust.
  - PIO flux_reader measures full period (pulse + gap)
  - CRC-16/CCITT on ID and data fields
  - Static PLL with half-cell tracking
  - 500ms read timeout, single external retry
  - Core 0: USB MSC + CDC debug + LED (RGB)
  - Core 1: pure floppy I/O, no peripherals
  - Step 3ms/3ms, settling 8ms, motor spin-up 500ms
  - DIP switch mode flags (debug/write/greasweasel)
  - WP pin + DIP switch write-protect layering
  - Composite USB device (MSC + CDC ACM)
  - DEBUG.md reference for serial output

DONE: write corruption fixes (4 bugs)
  1. emit_byte_a1() bit4: clock present [1,0] → should be absent [0,0]
     (prev=1 from bit5=1, so clock must be 0).  Fixed in mfm_encoder.cpp.
  2. PIO out_shift direction: shift_right=true output LSB-first but
     encoder packs MSB-first, reversing every 32-bit word.  Fixed in
     flux_writer.pio (changed to shift_right=false).
  3. Second CRC byte prev chaining: used (crc>>7)&1 instead of
     (crc>>8)&1, wrong clock context for LSB CRC byte.  Fixed.
  4. PIO clock divider: clkdiv=10 gave 1us half-cells, but decoder
     PLL=200 targets 2us.  Changed to clkdiv=20.  Fixed.

DONE: low-level track formatting
  - format_track_encode(): IBM-format track with 18 sectors, proper
    gaps (GAP4a 80, GAP1 50, GAP2 22, GAP3 66), 0xE5 data fill,
    CRC-16/CCITT on ID and data fields.
  - format_physical_track(): syncs on INDEX, writes full track in
    one revolution via PIO.
  - Debug serial command 'F' triggers full-disk format (80×2 tracks).
  - Progress output on CDC ACM serial.
  - tud_task() runs during track waits to keep USB alive.

